    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2501.13693v1</id>
    <title>A study of a recursive sequence of polynomials revealing weighted Catalan Numbers</title>
    <updated>2025-01-23T14:17:16Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.13693v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2501.13693v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>This paper examines the recursive sequence of polynomials $p_n(x)$, defined by $p_0(x) = x^2 - 2$ and $p_n(x) = p_{n-1}(x)^2 - 2$ for $n \geq 1$. It describes the field-theoretic motivations behind this sequence, derives a recursive formula for its coefficients, and identifies invariants that uncover combinatorial connections, including links to weighted Catalan numbers.</summary>
    <category term="math.CO" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
